gufo (0.15.1-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Build self-containment: add hip-dev and rocm-llvm to Build-Depends. The build runs
    find_package(hip), whose hip-config.cmake is shipped by hip-dev, and compiles .hip
    device code with ROCm's clang from rocm-llvm; without them dpkg-buildpackage fails on
    a machine that does not already happen to have them. python3 added for the same reason.
  * Build portability: the ROCm prefix is discovered with hipconfig --hip_path and can be
    overridden with DEB_ROCM_PREFIX, instead of assuming /opt/rocm.
  * Packaging: a marker written by prerm belongs to its own boot. Each marker records the
    boot id and postinst honours it only when it matches the running kernel's boot id;
    prerm clears markers before writing its own. A transaction that died between prerm and
    configure therefore cannot resurrect a unit an operator later stopped.
  * Tests: debian/tests/upgrade-units ships the 17-scenario lifecycle matrix as an
    autopkgtest. Runs against stubs - no real unit is touched, no root, no network - so
    the upgrade behaviour can be verified by anyone building this package.

 -- Gufo Maintainers <maintainers@gufo.dev>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:24:10 +0100

gufo (0.15.1-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Packaging: an upgrade no longer starts an instance an operator stopped.
    Enablement describes boot, not now: "inactive but enabled" was read as intent
    to run, so upgrading a host whose service was deliberately stopped brought it
    back up - binding its port, loading its weights, re-entering the balancer's
    path. `start' now requires a boot id recorded by prerm outside /run
    (/var/lib/gufo/upgrade-boot.id) that differs from the current one; the record
    is consumed once, so a reboot that predates the upgrade cannot start anything.

  * **cache:** avoid artifact hashing for RAM-only Flash-Next (#602)
  * **cache:** repair flash-next functional cache regressions (#596)

 -- Gufo Maintainers <maintainers@gufo.dev>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:31:09 +0100

